# Build output is not committed. `target/` is cargo's; `bin/` holds the release
# binary rebuilt by hand (`npx vite build` → `cargo build --release -p hearth-cli`
# → copy), because the binary embeds web/dist and cargo knows nothing about that.
# See docs/13-handover.md "Rebuilding the binary".
#
# Historical note: this used to say the target directory must leave the tree
# because the checkout path contained non-ASCII characters and cl.exe cannot
# write a debug record into such a path. The checkout is ASCII now (D:\hearth),
# so building in place is fine. The rule survives for the case where the tree is
# moved somewhere non-ASCII: set CARGO_TARGET_DIR then — see AGENTS.md.
/target
/bin
*.exe
*.pdb
*.dSYM

# Scratch space for probes and local experiments.
/.cache

# Nothing here is generated into the source tree; if it appears, it is a mistake.
**/dist/

# The desktop shell is its own cargo workspace, so its build output lands inside
# the tree instead of in /target, and `tauri-build` writes schemas on every build.
/apps/desktop/target
/apps/desktop/gen
